/* Theme section - Design tokens and theme variables
 *
 * NOTE: This file is part of the modular CSS organization but is not directly
 * imported (Textual CSS doesn't support @import). Instead, this content is
 * included in index.tcss under the "THEME" section.
 *
 * This file serves as documentation and reference for theme-related styles.
 */

/* Theme variables and design tokens - DESIGN SYSTEM */

/* NOTE: Textual provides built-in design tokens via $variables.
   This file documents which tokens are used throughout the app.
   See: https://textual.textualize.io/guide/design/#design-tokens */

/* Textual built-in tokens used:
   - $surface: Background color
   - $surface-lighten-1: Lighter background for hover states
   - $surface-darken-1: Darker background for nested content
   - $panel: Panel background
   - $primary: Primary accent color (blue/cyan)
   - $text: Normal text color
   - $text-muted: Secondary/muted text
   - $success: Success state color (green)
   - $warning: Warning state color (yellow)
   - $error: Error state color (red)
*/

/* Custom extensions could be added here if needed:
   - Custom color variables
   - Spacing scale overrides
   - Typography tokens
   - Border definitions
   - Shadow definitions
*/
